WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.580
- So a judge rules that the Trump campaign

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.460
non-disclosure agreement,
the NDA, is invalid.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.300
The story behind this
particular case is incredible.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.250
It's been going on for years but,

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.340
Jessica Denson most recently has filed

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.600
a class-action lawsuit

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.300
to invalidate the Trump campaign's NDA

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.570
that was preventing her from disclosing

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:20.050
what she saw and learned

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:21.920
as a member of the Trump campaign.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.300
So at the moment, at least
one federal court has said

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.660
that her particular NDA
is non-enforceable but

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.550
she's filed this as a class action

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.780
and it appears that she and her lawyers

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:34.640
intend to move forward and
invalidate all of the NDAs

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:35.990
with respect to the people

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:37.340
that worked for the Trump campaign.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.180
So this is not the last that we have heard

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:40.360
of this particular lawsuit.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:41.990
It may eventually go up
to the Court of Appeals,

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:42.823
but for the time being,

00:00:42.823 --> 00:00:44.130
it doesn't look good
for the Trump campaign.

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:46.553
So we'll see them in court.

